        <p class="result-hint" id="result-hint" hidden>
          Using the generic CBSE/UGC formula. <a href="/cgpa-to-percentage-chart">See all university formulas →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="trust-line">Free · No login · Formulas from official university circulars.</p>

  <a class="tools-link" href="/guides">Need CGPA to GPA, SGPA, or marks conversion? See all tools →</a>

  <section class="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading">
    <h2 id="how-it-works-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="how-steps">
      <li class="how-step"><span class="how-step-num">1</span><span>Pick your university so the calculator uses the formula your university publishes.</span></li>
      <li class="how-step"><span class="how-step-num">2</span><span>Type the CGPA printed on your marksheet, out of 10.</span></li>
      <li class="how-step"><span class="how-step-num">3</span><span>Read your percentage instantly — the exact formula used is shown below it.</span></li>
    </ol>
